#: ../../../intro/install.rst:17
msgid "Installing Scrapy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:19
msgid "Install Scrapy and its dependencies from PyPI with::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:21
msgid "pip install scrapy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:23
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend that you install Scrapy in :ref:`a dedicated virtual "
"environment <intro-using-virtualenv>`, to avoid conflicting with your system "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:27
msgid "Alternatively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:29
msgid ""
"From a `uv`_ project, e.g. one created with ``uv init``. ``uv`` manages the "
"virtual environment for you::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:32
msgid "uv add scrapy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:34
msgid "From the `conda-forge`_ channel, with ``conda``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:36
msgid "conda install -c conda-forge scrapy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:38
msgid ""
"If the installation fails while building one of the dependencies, see :ref:"
"`install-no-wheel`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:43
msgid "Things that are good to know"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:45
msgid ""
"Scrapy is written in pure Python and depends on a few key Python packages "
"(among others):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:47
msgid "`lxml`_, an efficient XML and HTML parser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:48
msgid "`parsel`_, an HTML/XML data extraction library written on top of lxml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:49
msgid ""
"`w3lib`_, a multi-purpose helper for dealing with URLs and web page encodings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:50
msgid "`twisted`_, an asynchronous networking framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:51
msgid ""
"`cryptography`_ and `pyOpenSSL`_, to deal with various network-level "
"security needs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:53
msgid ""
"Some of these packages include compiled code. They provide binary wheels for "
"common platforms, so that installing them requires no compiler; see :ref:"
"`install-no-wheel` if no wheel matches your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:61
msgid "Using a virtual environment (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:63
msgid ""
"TL;DR: We recommend installing Scrapy inside a virtual environment on all "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:66
msgid ""
"Python packages can be installed either globally (a.k.a. system-wide), or in "
"user-space. We do not recommend installing Scrapy system-wide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:69
msgid ""
"Instead, we recommend that you install Scrapy within a so-called \"virtual "
"environment\" (:mod:`venv`). Virtual environments allow you to avoid "
"conflicts with already-installed Python system packages (which could break "
"some of your system tools and scripts), and still install packages normally "
"with ``pip`` (without ``sudo`` or similar tools)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:75
msgid "See :ref:`tut-venv` on how to create your virtual environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:77
msgid ""
"Once you have created a virtual environment, you can install Scrapy inside "
"it with ``pip``, just like any other Python package."
msgstr ""

