#: ../../../intro/install.rst:140
msgid "Platform-specific installation notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:146
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:148
msgid ""
"Install Scrapy :ref:`as described above <intro-install-scrapy>`. "
"Dependencies that include compiled code provide wheels for 64-bit x86 "
"Windows, so no compiler is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:152
msgid ""
"On 32-bit or ARM64 Windows some of those wheels are missing, see :ref:"
"`install-no-wheel`. An additional option there is `WSL`_, which lets you "
"follow the :ref:`Linux instructions <install-linux>` instead. Note that your "
"code then runs on Linux, so Windows paths do not work in settings like :"
"setting:`FEEDS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:162
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:164
msgid ""
"Install Scrapy :ref:`as described above <intro-install-scrapy>`. "
"Dependencies that include compiled code provide ``manylinux`` and "
"``musllinux`` wheels, so no compiler is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:168
msgid ""
"**Don't** use the Scrapy package provided by your distribution, e.g. "
"``python-scrapy`` on Debian and Ubuntu, they are typically too old and slow "
"to catch up with the latest Scrapy release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:176
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:178
msgid ""
"Install Scrapy :ref:`as described above <intro-install-scrapy>`. "
"Dependencies that include compiled code provide wheels for both Intel and "
"Apple silicon, so no compiler is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:182
msgid ""
"We recommend against using the Python interpreter that comes with macOS. "
"Install a separate one instead, e.g. with `homebrew`_::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:185
msgid "brew install python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:192
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:197
msgid "Installation fails while building a dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:199
msgid ""
"When ``pip`` finds no wheel matching your Python version and platform, it "
"builds the dependency from its source distribution instead, which requires a "
"build toolchain and the libraries that the dependency wraps. To check "
"whether that is what fails for you, ask ``pip`` for wheels only::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:204
msgid "pip install --only-binary :all: scrapy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:206
msgid "With ``uv``, use ``uv add --no-build scrapy`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:208
msgid ""
"If that fails, no wheel is available, and you have the following options, "
"easiest first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:211
msgid ""
"Use an older Python version. Wheels for a new Python version may take weeks "
"to become available after its release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:214
msgid ""
"Use ``conda``, e.g. through `Miniforge`_, and install Scrapy from the `conda-"
"forge`_ channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:217
msgid ""
"Build the dependency from source, following its own installation "
"instructions, e.g. `lxml installation`_ or :doc:`cryptography installation "
"<cryptography:installation>`. Beyond a C compiler, this may require a Rust "
"compiler, development files of libraries like libxml2 or OpenSSL, or both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:223
msgid "AttributeError: 'module' object has no attribute 'OP_NO_TLSv1_1'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:225
msgid ""
"After you install or upgrade Scrapy, Twisted or pyOpenSSL, you may get an "
"exception with the following traceback::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:228
msgid ""
"[…]\n"
"  File \"[…]/site-packages/twisted/protocols/tls.py\", line 63, in <module>\n"
"    from twisted.internet._sslverify import _setAcceptableProtocols\n"
"  File \"[…]/site-packages/twisted/internet/_sslverify.py\", line 38, in "
"<module>\n"
"    TLSVersion.TLSv1_1: SSL.OP_NO_TLSv1_1,\n"
"AttributeError: 'module' object has no attribute 'OP_NO_TLSv1_1'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:235
msgid ""
"The reason you get this exception is that your system or virtual environment "
"has a version of pyOpenSSL that your version of Twisted does not support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:238
msgid ""
"To install a version of pyOpenSSL that your version of Twisted supports, "
"reinstall Twisted with the :code:`tls` extra option::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:241
msgid "pip install twisted[tls]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/install.rst:243
msgid ""
"For details, see `Issue #2473 <https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/"
"issues/2473>`_."
msgstr ""
